{
  "sentences": [
    {
      "i": 0,
      "revised": "Nowadays, transport is a very important issue in many countries.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "vocabulary", "punctuation"],
      "explanation": "原句缺少冠词和名词单复数错误（many country），且“problem”搭配不当；改为“a very important issue in many countries”更准确、正式。"
    },
    {
      "i": 1,
      "revised": "Some people think that governments should spend money on public transport rather than on building new roads.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "collocation", "spelling"],
      "explanation": "拼写错误（goverment）、介词搭配错误（spend money for→on）、动词形式错误（for build→on building），并补充that引导宾语从句，使句子符合Band 7语法要求。"
    },
    {
      "i": 2,
      "revised": "I partly agree with this opinion, but not entirely.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "clarity"],
      "explanation": "“I am agree”是典型语法错误，agree是动词不能与be连用；改为“I partly agree...but not entirely”更简洁清晰。"
    },
    {
      "i": 3,
      "revised": "Firstly, public transport is beneficial for people.",
      "tags": ["vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "“good for people”过于口语化，改为“beneficial for people”更符合学术写作语域。"
    },
    {
      "i": 4,
      "revised": "This is because many people do not have cars and they need buses and trains to go to work and school.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "punctuation", "spelling"],
      "explanation": "原句以Because开头构成不完整句，改为“This is because...”使其成为完整句；补充冠词和复数（cars, buses, trains），并修正拼写（dont→do not）。"
    },
    {
      "i": 5,
      "revised": "If buses were better, more people would use them and there would be less traffic.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "原句使用“more better”双重比较级错误，且时态不一致；改为虚拟语气“were...would use...would be”更准确，同时“less traffic”比“traffic will be less”更自然。"
    },
    {
      "i": 6,
      "revised": "In my city, buses are always late and very crowded, so people do not like to take them.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "collocation", "punctuation"],
      "explanation": "修正主谓一致（bus is→buses are）、用词错误（crowd→crowded）、拼写（dont→do not），并添加逗号使句子更清晰。"
    },
    {
      "i": 7,
      "revised": "Also, trains are too expensive for students.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "punctuation"],
      "explanation": "修正单复数（train→trains, student→students）并添加逗号，使句子更规范。"
    },
    {
      "i": 8,
      "revised": "Therefore, the government should make public transport cheaper and faster.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "vocabulary", "spelling"],
      "explanation": "修正拼写（goverment→government），用“Therefore”替代“So”更正式，并将“make it cheap and more fast”改为“make public transport cheaper and faster”更准确。"
    },
    {
      "i": 9,
      "revised": "Secondly, new roads are also important.",
      "tags": ["grammar"],
      "explanation": "修正主谓一致（road is→roads are），使句子语法正确。"
    },
    {
      "i": 10,
      "revised": "This is because the city is growing and more people are buying cars every year.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "punctuation"],
      "explanation": "原句以Because开头不完整，改为“This is because...”使其完整；修正动词形式（grow→growing, buy→are buying）使时态更准确。"
    },
    {
      "i": 11,
      "revised": "If there were no new roads, traffic jams would be very bad and people would waste a lot of time.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "collocation"],
      "explanation": "使用虚拟语气“were...would be...would waste”更准确，并将“traffic jam”改为复数“traffic jams”更自然。"
    },
    {
      "i": 12,
      "revised": "For example, my father drives to work every day and he spends two hours on the road.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "punctuation"],
      "explanation": "修正主谓一致（drive→drives, spend→spends）、名词单复数（hour→hours）并添加逗号，使句子更规范。"
    },
    {
      "i": 13,
      "revised": "This is very bad for him and for the economy as well.",
      "tags": ["vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "将“also”改为“as well”更符合句末位置，表达更自然。"
    },
    {
      "i": 14,
      "revised": "However, I think public transport is more important than roads.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "cohesion"],
      "explanation": "用“However”替代“But”更正式，并修正单复数（road→roads），使对比更清晰。"
    },
    {
      "i": 15,
      "revised": "This is because roads encourage more cars and more pollution.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "collocation"],
      "explanation": "原句以Because开头不完整，改为“This is because...”使其完整；将“make”改为“encourage”更准确，并修正主谓一致（road make→roads encourage）。"
    },
    {
      "i": 16,
      "revised": "Public transport can carry many people at one time and it is good for the environment.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "spelling", "collocation"],
      "explanation": "修正拼写（enviroment→environment），将“in one time”改为“at one time”更自然，并去掉不必要的冠词“The”。"
    },
    {
      "i": 17,
      "revised": "Also, if more people took buses, the city would be quieter and the air would be cleaner, so everybody could be healthier and happier.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "使用虚拟语气“took...would be...could be”更准确，并将形容词改为比较级（quieter, cleaner, healthier, happier）使表达更精确。"
    },
    {
      "i": 18,
      "revised": "In conclusion, I think governments should spend more money on public transport but also build some roads when it is necessary.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "collocation", "spelling"],
      "explanation": "修正拼写（goverment→governments），介词搭配（for→on），并修正单复数（road→roads），使句子更准确。"
    },
    {
      "i": 19,
      "revised": "Both are important for people and for the development of the country.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "修正主谓一致（Both is→Both are），并将“country develop”改为名词短语“the development of the country”更符合语法。"
    }
  ],
  "summary": "最频繁的问题包括：主谓一致错误（如many country, road make）、冠词和名词单复数缺失（如car, bus, road）、以及句子结构不完整（如以Because开头）。此外，拼写错误（goverment, enviroment）和介词搭配不当（spend money for）也较常见。"
}

{
  "sentences": [
    {
      "i": 0,
      "revised": "In many cities, traffic congestion has become a serious problem, and governments must decide how to allocate limited budgets.",
      "tags": ["vocabulary", "collocation"],
      "explanation": "“use limited budgets”搭配不够地道，改为“allocate limited budgets”更符合学术写作中关于预算分配的常用表达。"
    },
    {
      "i": 1,
      "revised": "Some people argue that money should be directed to public transport rather than to new roads.",
      "tags": ["collocation", "clarity"],
      "explanation": "“go to”过于口语化，改为“be directed to”更正式；同时补全“rather than to new roads”使比较结构更清晰。"
    },
    {
      "i": 2,
      "revised": "I largely agree with this view, although I believe that some road building is still necessary.",
      "tags": ["vocabulary", "grammar"],
      "explanation": "“mostly”改为“largely”更正式；在“believe”后加“that”引导宾语从句，使句子结构更完整。"
    },
    {
      "i": 3,
      "revised": "The main reason to invest in public transport is that it can move a large number of people efficiently.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 4,
      "revised": "A single train can carry hundreds of passengers, whereas the same number of people would require hundreds of cars.",
      "tags": ["cohesion", "vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "“while”改为“whereas”更准确地表达对比关系；“need”改为“require”更正式。"
    },
    {
      "i": 5,
      "revised": "If buses and trains are frequent, affordable and reliable, many drivers will choose them, which will reduce traffic jams.",
      "tags": ["vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "“cheap”改为“affordable”更符合学术语境，避免过于口语化。"
    },
    {
      "i": 6,
      "revised": "For example, after my city opened a new metro line, the main road to the city centre became much less congested during rush hour.",
      "tags": ["vocabulary", "collocation"],
      "explanation": "“crowded”用于道路不够准确，改为“congested”更符合交通语境。"
    },
    {
      "i": 7,
      "revised": "Another advantage is the environmental benefit.",
      "tags": ["clarity", "vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "“the environment”作为优势表述不完整，改为“the environmental benefit”使意思更明确。"
    },
    {
      "i": 8,
      "revised": "Cars produce a lot of air pollution and carbon emissions, which are harmful to people's health and contribute to climate change.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 9,
      "revised": "Public transport produces less pollution per passenger, so it is a more sustainable option in the long term.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 10,
      "revised": "On the other hand, new roads are sometimes necessary.",
      "tags": ["vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "“needed”改为“necessary”更正式，且与上文“necessary”呼应。"
    },
    {
      "i": 11,
      "revised": "In rural areas, there are not enough passengers to make train lines profitable, so people depend on cars.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 12,
      "revised": "Also, goods are mostly transported by trucks, and poor roads can slow down the economy.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 13,
      "revised": "In conclusion, I agree that governments should give priority to public transport because it is more efficient and better for the environment.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 14,
      "revised": "However, they should still build roads in places where public transport is not practical.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    }
  ],
  "summary": "主要问题集中在词汇正式度不足（如go to、cheap、crowded）和搭配不够地道（如use budgets）；部分句子结构可更完整（如believe后加that）。整体语法较好，但需提升学术表达的一致性。"
}

