      "revised": "Online learning has grown rapidly over the past decade, and many people now believe that it will eventually replace traditional classrooms.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 1,
      "revised": "In my view, although online courses offer clear advantages, face-to-face education will remain essential.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 2,
      "revised": "The most obvious benefit of online learning is flexibility.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 3,
      "revised": "Students can watch lectures at any time and study at their own pace, which is especially useful for adults who work full-time or have family responsibilities.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 4,
      "revised": "Online courses can also reach learners in remote areas who would otherwise have no access to good teachers.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 5,
      "revised": "In addition, digital materials can be updated quickly, and learners can replay difficult explanations as many times as they need, which is impossible in a traditional lecture.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 6,
      "revised": "For many people, these features make online study cheaper and more convenient than attending a college in person.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 7,
      "revised": "However, classroom learning provides things that are difficult to replicate on a screen.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 8,
      "revised": "Teachers can notice immediately when a student is confused and adapt their explanations.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 9,
      "revised": "Students also develop social skills by working together, discussing ideas and building friendships, which are an important part of education, particularly for children.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 10,
      "revised": "Furthermore, many learners find it hard to stay motivated without the structure of a timetable and the presence of classmates.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 11,
      "revised": "Completion rates for many free online courses are notoriously low, which suggests that self-discipline is a serious obstacle.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 12,
      "revised": "In conclusion, online learning is a valuable supplement that makes education more accessible and flexible, but it is unlikely to replace traditional classrooms, which offer interaction, support and motivation that technology cannot fully provide.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    }
  ],
  "summary": "整体语言质量很高，未发现明显错误；主要优点包括句式多样、衔接自然、词汇准确。建议继续保持。"
}

{
  "sentences": [
    {
      "i": 0,
      "revised": "I agree that governments should spend more money on public transport than on new roads.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 1,
      "revised": "Public transport can carry many people at the same time, so it reduces traffic congestion in big cities.",
      "tags": ["collocation"],
      "explanation": "“Traffic jams”是口语化表达，学术写作中更常用“traffic congestion”，更符合Band 7的词汇要求。"
    },
    {
      "i": 2,
      "revised": "It is also cheaper for students and elderly people who do not have cars.",
      "tags": ["vocabulary", "clarity"],
      "explanation": "“Old people”不够礼貌且口语化，改为“elderly people”更正式、得体；同时“students and elderly people”并列更清晰。"
    },
    {
      "i": 3,
      "revised": "In addition, buses and trains produce less pollution than private cars, which is good for the environment and for public health.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 4,
      "revised": "However, new roads are still useful in the countryside, where there are not many buses.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "i": 5,
      "revised": "In conclusion, public transport should be the priority, but some roads are still necessary.",
      "tags": [],
      "explanation": ""
    }
  ],
  "summary": "主要问题集中在词汇和搭配上：口语化表达（如“traffic jams”“old people”）需要替换为更正式、得体的学术用语。语法和拼写基本正确，但词汇多样性有待提升。"
}

